# check-ui rule 20 (status-tone, B9-17, DS-06, VC9) allowlist: files whose spoil or danger tone really is food going off or a loss.
# Format: <exact path>   # <reason>. An entry without a reason is ignored. A file that only needs warn, info or neutral never goes here:
# its package converts it. Feature files are added by the package that converts their folder (for example features/today UseSoonTile,
# food, with B9-44).
web/src/ui/Gallery.tsx   # the primitives Gallery shows every tone as a specimen, spoil and danger included
web/src/ui/GalleryOverlays.tsx   # the Gallery's overlay specimens show the danger confirm dialogs (a loss)
web/src/features/ingredients/lib/impact.ts   # Delete Ingredient / Delete Supply is a destructive confirm (a loss), which keeps its danger tone (B9-48, SAFE-02)
web/src/features/ingredients/screens/IngredientScreen.tsx   # the More menu's Delete Ingredient / Delete Supply item is the destructive action (a loss) (B9-48, SAFE-02)
web/src/features/import/components/StartOverButton.tsx   # the Start over confirm loses every answer given so far: a destructive confirm keeps its danger tone (main-session ruling, B9-28)
web/src/features/recipes/lib/editorExit.ts   # B9-31: "Discard your changes?" is a destructive confirm (the changes are lost), danger as R1 and the safe-06 mock draw it
